  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat percentage of Faraday's flower-shop sales came from sunflower bouquets? Faraday owns a flower stall. Faraday's flower shop sold 50 bouquets during the week. 12 of the bouquets sold that week were sunflower bouquets.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "To find the percentage of sunflower bouquets sold:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{50}\\times 100\\% = 24\\%\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{24\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Faraday owns a flower shop.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "No problem—the calculation is unchanged. Faraday’s flower shop sold 50 bouquets, 12 of which were sunflower bouquets:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{50}\\times 100\\% = 24\\%\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{24\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Great. Now let's take that a step further. How many sunflower bouquets did Faraday sell per day on average during that week? Additionally, Faraday's flower shop was open for 6 days during that week.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Faraday sold 12 sunflower bouquets over 6 days. The average number sold per day was:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{6}=2\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2\\text{ sunflower bouquets per day}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: Faraday sells individual sunflowers for $3 each.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Understood. Individual sunflowers cost **$3 each**. This doesn’t change the average of **2 sunflower bouquets per day**; we’d need to know how many individual sunflowers were in each bouquet to calculate their value.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Good, now using that, can you calculate: How many sunflowers was Faraday able to sell after three days? And here are a few things you should know: Faraday sells bouquets of sunflowers for $8 each. Faraday earns $26 per day from individual sunflowers and $56 per day from bouquets.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "For individual sunflowers, Faraday earns:\n\n\\[\n26 \\text{ dollars per day}\\times 3=78\\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\nSince each sunflower sells for \\$3:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{78}{3}=26\n\\]\n\nSo, Faraday sold:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{26\\text{ individual sunflowers}}\n\\]\n\nFor reference, the bouquet sales would be:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{56}{8}\\times 3=21\\text{ bouquets}\n\\]\n\nThe exact number of individual flowers in those bouquets cannot be determined without knowing how many sunflowers each bouquet contains.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "One more thing — Each bouquet contains 12 sunflowers.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Over three days:\n\n1. **Individual sunflowers sold:**\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\$26 \\times 3}{\\$3}=26\\text{ sunflowers}\n\\]\n\n2. **Bouquets sold:**\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\$56 \\times 3}{\\$8}=21\\text{ bouquets}\n\\]\n\n3. **Sunflowers in the bouquets:**\n\n\\[\n21\\times 12=252\\text{ sunflowers}\n\\]\n\n4. **Total sunflowers:**\n\n\\[\n26+252=278\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{278\\text{ sunflowers}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Faraday sells individual sunflowers for $2 each.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "With individual sunflowers priced at **$2 each**:\n\n- Individual sunflower sales over 3 days:\n\n\\[\n\\$26 \\times 3=\\$78\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\$78\\div \\$2=39\\text{ individual sunflowers}\n\\]\n\n- Bouquet sales over 3 days:\n\n\\[\n\\$56\\times 3=\\$168\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\$168\\div \\$8=21\\text{ bouquets}\n\\]\n\n- Sunflowers in bouquets:\n\n\\[\n21\\times 12=252\n\\]\n\n- Total sunflowers sold:\n\n\\[\n39+252=291\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{291\\text{ sunflowers}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
